{
 "schema_version": 1,
 "description": "Waiting for a hub to admit a new connection: about ninety seconds while the platform carries the client to its hub. The wait follows the operation the create answered with, polling GET /v1/operations/{id} (its links.self) every poll_interval_ms, and no read may run past the wait's own deadline. 'ready' is 'admitted'; 'failed' and 'timed_out' are 'failed', with the operation's error_code and status null; requested, committed and applied keep polling. No operation at all, and a 404 (the API no longer tracks it), are 'admitted' at once. A 5xx is ridden out. So is a 429 (a Free plan allows 60 requests a minute): the next poll waits the problem's retry_after_seconds -- the API puts it inside the detail object, as api-errors reads code; read it at the top too -- else the Retry-After header, else RateLimit-Reset (the API's own rate limiter answers in plain text with only that header), or poll_interval_ms when that is longer or none is given; when that is more than the time left the outcome is 'timeout' at once. A 401 or 403 is 'auth': the API's own authentication error, passed through, never a failed admission. Any other refusal of the wait itself is 'failed' with error_code null and the api-errors status, code and detail. An API that cannot be reached is 'unreachable', the SDK's own error for that, never a failed admission (call.api 'unreachable' points the SDK at a port where nothing listens). When timeout_ms pass first the outcome is 'timeout', which is a connection error and a timeout at once, and whose message ends \"it may still admit it later\". A links.self whose origin -- scheme, host and port, the scheme's default port spelled out -- is not the API's is 'error' and is never fetched: the token goes nowhere else. In links.self, {api_host} and {api_port} stand for the host and port of the API the SDK is pointed at. polls counts the GETs sent; waited_at_least_ms, when present, is the least time the wait must have taken. Every duration is whole milliseconds; response headers are listed when the API sends any that matter.",
 "source": "thalovant-api app/routes/clients.py _accept_client_sync_operation, app/routes/operations.py, app/services/operation_convergence.py (#358); app/auth/deps.py (token_rate_limited, token_quota_exceeded), app/middleware/errors.py (the Problem+JSON envelope), app/middleware/ratelimit.py (the plain 429)",
